  "description": "T1 Horse Chestnut Tree: Re-Pollard back to previous Reason: Routine maintenance T2 Cherry Plum: Crown reduction by 2m on all aspects to tidy and contain shape Reason: Routine maintenance T3 Silver Birch: Crown reduction by 3.5m on all aspects to tidy and contain shape. Justification of Works: Amenity Management: The reduction will improve the tree's overall aesthetic appearance, in keeping with the surrounding maintained landscape. Proportional Balance: The works will help restore a balanced crown and prevent asymmetrical growth, especially where previous pruning or environmental factors may have caused uneven development. Preventative Maintenance: Reducing the crown will lessen the wind-loading on limbs, reducing the risk of limb failure during high winds or storms. Size Management: The current size of the tree is becoming disproportionate to the garden space and surrounding structures; a moderate reduction will help maintain its suitability within the plot. Good Arboricultural Practice: The works proposed are minor and within recommended guidance (less than 30% overall crown volume), ensuring long-term health and structure of the tree.",
